// Title: Enable Local Manifest Installation With Winget
// Sigma ID: fa277e82-9b78-42dd-b05c-05555c7b6015
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-04-17 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence, stealth
// Description: Detects changes to the AppInstaller (winget) policy. Specifically the activation of the local
//   manifest installation, which allows a user to install new packages via custom manifests.
// False positives:
//   - Administrators or developers might enable this for testing purposes or to install custom private packages
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20250828100901/https://github.com/nasbench/Misc-Research/tree/b9596e8109dcdb16ec353f316678927e507a5b8d/LOLBINs/Winget
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cb982537eb7397f93785ec066cce7b017050a43f/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_winget_enable_local_manifest.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\AppInstaller\\EnableLocalManifestFiles" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)"
